{{see also|Illinois's 3rd congressional district}}
During the 2020 redistricting process, the Illinois General Assembly decided to create a second Latino-influenced district. As such, the 3rd congressional district had no incumbent.<ref name=Draw>{{cite web|url=https://www.dailyherald.com/news/20211027/plan-to-radically-reshape-6th-congressional-district-is-drawing-criticism|title=Plan to radically reshape 6th Congressional District is drawing criticism|website=Daily Herald|last1=Lissau|first1=Russell|date=October 27, 2021|access-date=October 30, 2021|archive-date=October 30, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211030025554/https://www.dailyherald.com/news/20211027/plan-to-radically-reshape-6th-congressional-district-is-drawing-criticism|url-status=live}}</ref> The district is approximately 47% Latino and unites heavily Latino communities from Chicago to Elgin.<ref>{{cite news|last=Vinicky|first=Amanda|title=Illinois Lawmakers Approve New Congressional Map|date=October 29, 2021|publisher=[[WTTW]]|access-date=November 22, 2021|url=https://news.wttw.com/2021/10/29/illinois-lawmakers-approve-new-congressional-map|archive-date=November 23, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211123053541/https://news.wttw.com/2021/10/29/illinois-lawmakers-approve-new-congressional-map|url-status=live}}</ref> Among potential voters, the communities in the district include 63.4% White, 25.2% Latino, 6.2% Black, and 4.7% Asian people.<ref>{{cite web|title=Illinois' 3rd Congressional District election, 2022|url=https://ballotpedia.org/Illinois'_3rd_Congressional_District_election,_2022|website=Ballotpedia}}</ref> It includes parts of the Chicago neighborhoods of [[West Town, Chicago|West Town]], [[Logan Square, Chicago|Logan Square]], [[Humboldt Park, Chicago|Humboldt Park]], [[Belmont Cragin, Chicago|Belmont Cragin]], [[Portage Park, Chicago|Portage Park]], [[Irving Park, Chicago|Irving Park]], [[Albany Park, Chicago|Albany Park]], [[Montclare, Chicago|Montclare]], [[Dunning, Chicago|Dunning]], and all or parts of the suburbs of [[Elmwood Park, Illinois|Elmwood Park]], [[River Grove, Illinois|River Grove]], [[Franklin Park, Illinois|Franklin Park]], [[Bensenville, Illinois|Bensenville]], [[Elk Grove Village, Illinois|Elk Grove Village]], [[Wood Dale, Illinois|Wood Dale]], [[Addison, Illinois|Addison]], [[Glendale Heights, Illinois|Glendale Heights]], [[Wheaton, Illinois|Wheaton]], [[West Chicago, Illinois|West Chicago]], [[Wayne, Illinois|Wayne]], [[Bartlett, Illinois|Bartlett]], [[Hanover Park, Illinois|Hanover Park]], and [[Elgin, Illinois|Elgin]].<ref name="Final Map">{{cite web|title=Congressional Draft 4 10.29.2021|date=October 29, 2021|access-date=November 22, 2021|url=https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1DuemrWTVXzfvozXGm1Vts_nkTD5jXw9W&ll=41.94084779497774%2C-87.78960002748642&z=13|archive-date=November 23, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211123053531/https://www.google.com/maps/d/viewer?mid=1DuemrWTVXzfvozXGm1Vts_nkTD5jXw9W&ll=41.94084779497774,-87.78960002748642&z=13|url-status=live}}</ref>

