{{see also|Illinois's 15th congressional district}}
Incumbent Republican [[Mary Miller (politician)|Mary Miller]] then represented the 15th congressional district, and was running for re-election in the district. Due to redistricting, Republican [[Rodney Davis (politician)|Rodney Davis]], who represented the 13th congressional district, resided in the 15th district and opted to run in the new 15th district rather than the more Democratic 13th. The new 15th district, located in western and central Illinois, includes all or parts of [[Adams County, Illinois|Adams]], [[Bond County, Illinois|Bond]], [[Brown County, Illinois|Brown]], [[Calhoun County, Illinois|Calhoun]], [[Cass County, Illinois|Cass]], [[Coles County, Illinois|Coles]], [[DeWitt County, Illinois|DeWitt]], [[Edgar County, Illinois|Edgar]], [[Greene County, Illinois|Greene]], [[Hancock County, Illinois|Hancock]], [[Henderson County, Illinois|Henderson]], [[Jersey County, Illinois|Jersey]], [[Logan County, Illinois|Logan]], [[Macon County, Illinois|Macon]], [[Madison County, Illinois|Madison]], [[Mercer County, Illinois|Mercer]], [[Menard County, Illinois|Menard]], [[Montgomery County, Illinois|Montgomery]], [[Morgan County, Illinois|Morgan]], [[Pike County, Illinois|Pike]], [[Sangamon County, Illinois|Sangamon]], [[Schuyler County, Illinois|Schuyler]], [[Scott County, Illinois|Scott]], [[Shelby County, Illinois|Shelby]], [[Christian County, Illinois|Christian]], [[Vermillion County, Illinois|Vermillion]], and [[Warren County, Illinois|Warren]] counties.<ref name="Final Map"/>

